WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.310 --> 00:00:03.960
Someone was screaming inside the incinerator.

00:00:03.960 --> 00:00:05.390
The year was 1975.

00:00:05.390 --> 00:00:11.440
The location was a top secret refinery and
waste disposal plant, one of the many front

00:00:11.440 --> 00:00:15.940
organizations owned and operated by the SCP
Foundation.

00:00:15.940 --> 00:00:21.360
This sprawling facility, separated into three
different huge units, each with a specialized

00:00:21.360 --> 00:00:26.439
task, was located around 75 kilometers outside
of Summer Springs, Colorado.

00:00:26.439 --> 00:00:33.000
It had operated for several decades without
incident, but today, all hell was about to

00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:34.300
break loose.

00:00:34.300 --> 00:00:39.930
Alarms were blaring in Unit C, the area of
the facility that dealt with destroying non-anomalous

00:00:39.930 --> 00:00:41.390
waste via incineration.

00:00:41.390 --> 00:00:47.240
A traumatized worker had pulled the emergency
lever near one of the incinerators in a panic

00:00:47.240 --> 00:00:53.620
when he’d first heard the loud banging against
the interior walls, and then, those horrific,

00:00:53.620 --> 00:00:54.620
pained wails.

00:00:54.620 --> 00:01:00.330
That’s when the workers of Unit C came to
a horrifying realization: The screams weren’t

00:01:00.330 --> 00:01:05.859
just coming from one of the incinerators in
Unit C, they were coming from all six.

00:01:05.859 --> 00:01:12.280
A chorus of absolute agony, echoing up out
of the ash pits.

00:01:12.280 --> 00:01:16.579
This was impossible, as far as the Unit C
staff were concerned.

00:01:16.579 --> 00:01:21.630
These incinerators were only to be used for
confirmed non-anomalous material - could some

00:01:21.630 --> 00:01:25.829
animals or even some poor workers somehow
fallen into the incinerators?

00:01:25.829 --> 00:01:31.649
But even if they had, what were the odds that
someone had fallen in all six of them at once?

00:01:31.649 --> 00:01:33.969
It was impossible.

00:01:33.969 --> 00:01:38.340
The Site Director was immediately brought
in to authorize an investigation, at which

00:01:38.340 --> 00:01:43.469
point he demanded that at least one of the
furnaces - in this case, Furnace Number 4

00:01:43.469 --> 00:01:48.780
- be shut off so researchers and guards could
investigate what was going on inside.

00:01:48.780 --> 00:01:53.859
It seemed like the obvious course of action,
but for some of the people on site that day,

00:01:53.859 --> 00:01:56.009
this would prove to be a fatal mistake.

00:01:56.009 --> 00:02:00.709
When the fires were put out, something started
rattling in the disposal chute.

00:02:00.709 --> 00:02:06.500
There was a scratching and squealing noise,
like something scraping up against the metal.

00:02:06.500 --> 00:02:11.532
A maintenance worker was ordered to go check
inside, and when he opened the hatch, he let

00:02:11.532 --> 00:02:13.730
out a bone-chilling shriek.

00:02:13.730 --> 00:02:16.500
There was something - or was it someone?

00:02:16.500 --> 00:02:18.870
- climbing back up the disposal chute.

00:02:18.870 --> 00:02:24.239
It emerged from the darkness, backlit by the
still-burning embers of the incinerator, letting

00:02:24.239 --> 00:02:29.560
out an awful, screeching noise that could
make even a hardened Mobile Task Force operative

00:02:29.560 --> 00:02:31.329
shake with fear.

00:02:31.329 --> 00:02:37.360
The creature was humanoid, a charred, mutilated
skeleton, reaching out towards the maintenance

00:02:37.360 --> 00:02:39.450
worker with a bony claw.

00:02:39.450 --> 00:02:43.760
Before the worker had a chance to stumble
back in horror, the beast had clasped him

00:02:43.760 --> 00:02:45.879
by the throat and started to squeeze.

00:02:45.879 --> 00:02:51.189
It didn’t even need to strangle him - the
heat of its skeletal hand burned away the

00:02:51.189 --> 00:02:56.110
worker’s throat in seconds, leaving his
limp, wheezing body to drop to the metal grate

00:02:56.110 --> 00:02:58.459
of the platform below him.

00:02:58.459 --> 00:03:02.269
Several armed guards and maintenance workers
moved forward to fend off the monster, but

00:03:02.269 --> 00:03:07.159
just then a volley of more violent shrieks
echoed out of the chute behind it.

00:03:07.159 --> 00:03:11.530
It only took seconds for over a dozen more
creatures to crawl out of the disposal chute.

00:03:11.530 --> 00:03:17.849
They were all like the first - people at various
stages of incineration, some were glowing,

00:03:17.849 --> 00:03:24.360
charred skeletons with barely any flesh, others
looking more like severe burn victims, their

00:03:24.360 --> 00:03:28.709
faces contorted into scowls of hate and rage.

00:03:28.709 --> 00:03:33.810
The assembled guards opened fire on the sudden
influx of anomalies, emptying the magazines

00:03:33.810 --> 00:03:38.650
of their submachine guns into the burning
bodies, but their weapons didn’t seem to

00:03:38.650 --> 00:03:41.319
cause any lasting damage.

00:03:41.319 --> 00:03:45.150
The bullets would tear through the flesh of
the creatures, causing some of them to stumble

00:03:45.150 --> 00:03:50.269
and fall, but the wounds would close and the
creatures would rise again.

00:03:50.269 --> 00:03:54.740
It seemed they possessed a deadly combo of
extremely high aggression, and incredible

00:03:54.740 --> 00:03:56.359
regenerative abilities.

00:03:56.359 --> 00:04:01.709
None of the staff present in Unit C were safe
as the burned corpses attacked anyone they

00:04:01.709 --> 00:04:06.640
could find with their bare hands, beating
and biting and clawing.

00:04:06.640 --> 00:04:10.810
Many of them would grapple with Foundation
personnel, latching on to them and trying

00:04:10.810 --> 00:04:14.489
to pull them back down into the incinerator
with them.

00:04:14.489 --> 00:04:20.739
These creatures that would later be known
as SCP-2419-A caused several fatalities with

00:04:20.739 --> 00:04:25.900
their surprise attack that day, and the situation
was only brought back under control when a

00:04:25.900 --> 00:04:31.139
Mobile Task Force that possessed more advanced
training and weaponry was dispatched to the

00:04:31.139 --> 00:04:32.139
location.

00:04:32.139 --> 00:04:37.210
Despite orders from the Site Director, the
MTF found it impossible to actually terminate

00:04:37.210 --> 00:04:40.900
any of the entities due to their regenerative
abilities.

00:04:40.900 --> 00:04:46.710
Instead, the MTF agents focused on forcing
the anomalies back into the chute of Incinerator

00:04:46.710 --> 00:04:50.800
Number 4 using a powerful industrial steam
lance.

00:04:50.800 --> 00:04:55.320
Once they were back inside, the incinerator’s
burners were started up once again.

00:04:55.320 --> 00:04:59.950
The MTF were also able to capture five of
the entities and detain them for questioning

00:04:59.950 --> 00:05:05.710
and experimentation, finally bringing this
unexpected containment breach to an end.

00:05:05.710 --> 00:05:10.880
The Foundation is an organization that prides
itself on possessing forbidden and secret

00:05:10.880 --> 00:05:14.820
knowledge, but even they had no idea what
had just happened.

00:05:14.820 --> 00:05:19.570
There seemed to be no earthly explanation
why these creatures would suddenly manifest

00:05:19.570 --> 00:05:25.610
inside the incinerators, but as the detained
anomalies continued regenerating, a slightly

00:05:25.610 --> 00:05:31.250
clearer picture of what exactly the Foundation
was dealing with began to emerge.

00:05:31.250 --> 00:05:35.340
Every single one of the captured anomalies
kept regenerating, and upon getting to the

00:05:35.340 --> 00:05:40.509
point that they were no-longer burn scarred,
the researchers studying the anomalous creatures

00:05:40.509 --> 00:05:45.610
discovered that each one was identical to
a deceased D-Class from the Foundation’s

00:05:45.610 --> 00:05:46.610
records.

00:05:46.610 --> 00:05:51.169
They were physically and genetically identical
to the dead Class D Personnel.

00:05:51.169 --> 00:05:55.879
Perfect copies, save for the fact that their
sole mission in life seemed to now be pure

00:05:55.879 --> 00:05:59.849
and unmitigated aggression and violence.

00:05:59.849 --> 00:06:03.389
Researchers wanted to gain greater insight
into the minds of these strange creatures

00:06:03.389 --> 00:06:07.340
through the use of extensive psychological
evaluations and interviews.

00:06:07.340 --> 00:06:11.300
It would turn out to be a very dangerous investigation.

00:06:11.300 --> 00:06:16.259
A psychological researcher by the name of
Dr. Warren conducted an interview with one

00:06:16.259 --> 00:06:22.220
of the SCP-2419-A instances in hopes of better
understanding their mindset.

00:06:22.220 --> 00:06:27.319
This creature had been heard laughing not
long before the interview began, so it wasn’t

00:06:27.319 --> 00:06:31.919
an unreasonable assumption to believe that
it could be capable of speech.

00:06:31.919 --> 00:06:36.340
The interviewee was separated from Dr. Warren
by a thick pane of glass to prevent it from

00:06:36.340 --> 00:06:39.509
indulging in any of its more violent urges.

00:06:39.509 --> 00:06:45.440
The problem was that Dr. Warren and his assistant
researchers had severely underestimated what

00:06:45.440 --> 00:06:49.280
these creatures were capable of doing to get
what they wanted.

00:06:49.280 --> 00:06:52.780
Dr. Warren tried to begin the interview in
good faith.

00:06:52.780 --> 00:06:57.750
He spoke calmly and politely to the creature
through the glass, attempting to remind it

00:06:57.750 --> 00:06:59.979
of the person it once was.

00:06:59.979 --> 00:07:04.800
The anomaly didn’t appear to be paying attention
to the doctor though, instead focusing on

00:07:04.800 --> 00:07:09.190
pulling its own arm apart, and breaking the
bones within.

00:07:09.190 --> 00:07:14.129
Dr. Warren began to think that the creatures
weren’t even sentient, if the only activity

00:07:14.129 --> 00:07:18.880
they seemed to engage in was the wanton destruction
of themselves and others.

00:07:18.880 --> 00:07:23.220
But underestimating them like this proved
to be a big mistake.

00:07:23.220 --> 00:07:28.230
By removing the skin off of its arm, and whittling
its bones down to sharp edges, the anomaly

00:07:28.230 --> 00:07:31.680
had transformed its arm into a makeshift knife.

00:07:31.680 --> 00:07:35.889
Before anyone realized this, it had already
used its own jagged bones to break the glass

00:07:35.889 --> 00:07:38.250
divider and attack Dr. Warren.

00:07:38.250 --> 00:07:43.819
He perished not long after, after being stabbed
multiple times in his face and eyes and the

00:07:43.819 --> 00:07:46.639
anomaly was forcefully taken back to its holding
cell.

00:07:46.639 --> 00:07:50.849
Dr. Daniel Jennings, a senior researcher,
was then put on the case.

00:07:50.849 --> 00:07:55.440
He released a chilling memo on the creatures
after his observation period ended.

00:07:55.440 --> 00:07:56.440
It read:

00:07:56.440 --> 00:07:59.259
“Before I came here, I worked as a prison
shrink.

00:07:59.259 --> 00:08:03.240
Every person you met had a story bursting
with pain and sorrow.

00:08:03.240 --> 00:08:07.530
Sometimes, those stories were about the pain
they suffered; sometimes, it was about the

00:08:07.530 --> 00:08:09.650
pain they inflicted.

00:08:09.650 --> 00:08:15.119
Some days you felt like everyone there was
a beautiful soul torn down by their circumstances

00:08:15.119 --> 00:08:20.110
— other days, you'd find out what some of
them did and a part of you was glad they were

00:08:20.110 --> 00:08:21.430
there to suffer for it.

00:08:21.430 --> 00:08:26.460
But at the end of every day, I always told
myself: They're all humans.

00:08:26.460 --> 00:08:27.729
They're all people.

00:08:27.729 --> 00:08:33.029
They all deserve the same dignity, respect,
and love as everyone else.

00:08:33.029 --> 00:08:34.560
No exceptions.”

00:08:34.560 --> 00:08:36.060
Dr. Jennings goes on.

00:08:36.060 --> 00:08:40.520
“I opened up with that anecdote only so
you could understand that what I'm about to

00:08:40.520 --> 00:08:45.810
say is not said lightly: These things are
not people.

00:08:45.810 --> 00:08:48.070
They are people-shaped monsters.

00:08:48.070 --> 00:08:52.610
They are well beyond any definition of psychopathy.

00:08:52.610 --> 00:08:56.830
Everything they do, they do to hurt, maim,
and kill.

00:08:56.830 --> 00:09:01.460
I would pity them, but that would imply that
they're worth pitying.

00:09:01.460 --> 00:09:05.170
Put them in a hole, then fill that hole with
concrete.

00:09:05.170 --> 00:09:09.420
Better still: Throw them back into the incinerator
where you found them.

00:09:09.420 --> 00:09:11.680
I doubt they'll even care.”

00:09:11.680 --> 00:09:16.180
Following this string of unfortunate incidents,
containment procedures were put into place

00:09:16.180 --> 00:09:21.030
to hopefully prevent anything that had happened
to the unlucky Foundation staff from happening

00:09:21.030 --> 00:09:22.030
again.

00:09:22.030 --> 00:09:27.690
The entire facility was fenced off, and was
constantly patrolled by MTF Beta-7, also known

00:09:27.690 --> 00:09:33.089
as the Maz Hatters, a group specializing in
containing anomalies which present powerful

00:09:33.089 --> 00:09:36.670
biological, chemical, or radiological dangers.

00:09:36.670 --> 00:09:41.610
The furnaces that the anomalous creatures
emerged from remain lit at all times, with

00:09:41.610 --> 00:09:47.370
workers checking and carrying out maintenance
on every single one, each day of the week.

00:09:47.370 --> 00:09:51.210
Outside of this, the facility is essentially
a no-go zone.

00:09:51.210 --> 00:09:56.760
Reinforced steel hatches cover the chutes,
and they are to forever remain bolted shut.

00:09:56.760 --> 00:10:01.160
All because of that one terrifying day in
1975.

00:10:01.160 --> 00:10:07.320
That was the day that the Summer Springs waste
disposal facility, which had been a valuable

00:10:07.320 --> 00:10:13.430
asset to the Foundation for decades, instead
became classified as the Euclid-Class anomaly

00:10:13.430 --> 00:10:14.970
SCP-2419.

00:10:14.970 --> 00:10:21.600
It’s not uncommon for a Foundation asset
to one day become a dangerous anomaly requiring

00:10:21.600 --> 00:10:24.779
containment, but the same question always
pops up after...

00:10:24.779 --> 00:10:25.779
Why?

00:10:25.779 --> 00:10:30.250
Why had a place that had been so valuable
to the Foundation suddenly become such an

00:10:30.250 --> 00:10:31.760
active danger?

00:10:31.760 --> 00:10:36.510
The answer, as is often the case, is contained
within the question.

00:10:36.510 --> 00:10:41.459
Why would a waste disposal plant be so important
to the Foundation in the first place?

00:10:41.459 --> 00:10:46.190
And more importantly, what else was going
on at the plant to make it such an area of

00:10:46.190 --> 00:10:51.820
active importance for one of the most powerful
organizations in the entire world?

00:10:51.820 --> 00:10:57.300
To put it simply, the plant allowed the Foundation
to dispose of something far more important

00:10:57.300 --> 00:11:03.480
than mere waste material - it gave them what
they needed to better erase memories.

00:11:03.480 --> 00:11:08.390
As you probably already know, the Foundation
makes liberal use of amnestics on those exposed

00:11:08.390 --> 00:11:14.310
to anomalous material to make them forget
what they have seen and experienced, but these

00:11:14.310 --> 00:11:20.220
elusive chemicals - many of which are sourced
from SCP-3000 - are an inexact science.

00:11:20.220 --> 00:11:25.110
However, at the Summer Springs waste disposal
plant, researchers discovered an immensely

00:11:25.110 --> 00:11:27.209
valuable alternative.

00:11:27.209 --> 00:11:32.149
Much of what was disposed of in the incinerators
of Unit C were the bodies of dead D-Class

00:11:32.149 --> 00:11:33.470
personnel.

00:11:33.470 --> 00:11:38.420
Before being burned, autopsies were performed
on the bodies to make sure they were non-anomalous

00:11:38.420 --> 00:11:40.570
- including the brain.

00:11:40.570 --> 00:11:45.590
Back in the 1960s, while performing research
on the brains of the dead D-Classes, they

00:11:45.590 --> 00:11:50.139
found a method of extracting and distilling
the positive memories of the dead, creating

00:11:50.139 --> 00:11:52.670
a kind of “Happy Soup.”

00:11:52.670 --> 00:11:58.010
When administered into someone who has undergone
amnestic treatment, this happy soup creates

00:11:58.010 --> 00:12:02.779
positive false memories in their mind that
fills in those pesky blank spaces that are

00:12:02.779 --> 00:12:04.860
often behind.

00:12:04.860 --> 00:12:09.480
This was so useful that happy memories were
extracted from the minds of every single D-Class

00:12:09.480 --> 00:12:14.399
corpse that passed through Unit C, totaling
well into the thousands by the time that the

00:12:14.399 --> 00:12:19.390
first SCP-2419-A instances began to rise.

00:12:19.390 --> 00:12:24.760
But as all happiness, joy, and love were removed
from the minds of the D-Classes, it seemed

00:12:24.760 --> 00:12:30.310
that all that was left was pure hate, pain,
violence, and fury.

00:12:30.310 --> 00:12:34.459
Feelings too intense and evil to destroy.

00:12:34.459 --> 00:12:39.410
These were bodies imbued with a malice so
powerful that no fire could ever burn them

00:12:39.410 --> 00:12:40.449
away.

00:12:40.449 --> 00:12:46.170
They exist now with single-minded determination
to get out and destroy everything around them.

00:12:46.170 --> 00:12:47.170
Everything.

00:12:47.170 --> 00:12:51.980
Including the ones that made them, the SCP
Foundation itself.

00:12:51.980 --> 00:12:56.070
And in the end, it’s only a matter of time
until they get out.

00:12:56.070 --> 00:13:02.120
There are thousands of them in there, unable
to die, unable to stop.

00:13:02.120 --> 00:13:07.339
The only thing keeping them in there is the
constant burning of the furnaces around them,

00:13:07.339 --> 00:13:10.190
and those furnaces can’t burn forever.

00:13:10.190 --> 00:13:16.110
The monsters lurking in SCP-2419 will outlive
the fire that surrounds them, because while

00:13:16.110 --> 00:13:22.920
the furnaces they are contained in are hot,
the fires of hate that burn within SCP2419

00:13:22.920 --> 00:13:24.940
entities are even more powerful.

00:13:24.940 --> 00:13:26.990
And they know this.

00:13:26.990 --> 00:13:32.339
They know they can’t be contained forever,
and that someday soon, they’ll be able to

00:13:32.339 --> 00:13:36.300
emerge and exact their terrible revenge.

00:13:36.300 --> 00:13:40.380
Those who must walk past the incinerators
may think they hear their screams echoing

00:13:40.380 --> 00:13:43.990
out from within, but it’s not screaming
at all.

00:13:43.990 --> 00:13:45.510
It’s laughter.

00:13:45.510 --> 00:13:51.730
Now check out “SCP-1861 - The Crew of the
HMS Wintersheimer” and “SCP-3999 - I Am

00:13:51.730 --> 00:13:56.620
At The Center of Everything That Happens To
Me” for more Tales of Terror from the SCP

00:13:56.620 --> 00:13:57.120
Foundation!

